hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"141","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhni said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, some riders appeared. When we saw them, he said: ""These are the people of Muzayjijah."" Then some men from Muzayjijah came. He said: ""I will go to them to make a covenant with them."" He took hold of one of them and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! See who has come to see you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you. What is his reward?"" He said: ""For him is forgiveness."" He then patted him on the hand and turned away. Then another man came, and he took hold of him, saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! See who has come to see you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you, but did not see you."" He said: ""For him is forgiveness, then for him is forgiveness, then for him is forgiveness."" He then patted him on the hand and turned away."
"142","We were sitting with al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad one day when a man passed by us. He said, ""Peace be upon those who have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and upon Allah! If only we had seen what he saw and witnessed what he witnessed, we would have been more pleased. I would have been more pleased, and I would have said only good. Then he turned to us and said, 'What burdens the man who is given to forgetfulness, for Allah has hidden it from him. He does not know how it will be in him, and Allah has prepared a people for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who will be taken up to their graves in the morning, and their Lord will not respond to them, nor will He acknowledge them. They will not thank Allah when He brings them out, nor will they recognize their Lord when He brings them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that their Lord has brought them out. They will not know that their Lord has brought them out, and they will not know that 