"153","Musa bin Ali said, ""I heard my father say, 'I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As say, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say, ""Do you know what the Muslim is?"" They said, ""God and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The Muslim is he whose tongue and hand are pure."" He said, ""Do you know who the believer is?"" They said, ""God and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The believer is he who believes in Allah and His Messenger, and who migrates for the sake of Allah, and who flees from what Allah has forbidden.'"""
"154","The faithful believer is one who is filled with faith, and there is no good in one who is not filled with faith and is not filled with it."
"155","From Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) took my hand and said to me: ""O Abu Umama, indeed among the believers is one who will be pleased with his heart."""
"156","A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have memorized the Quran, but I do not find my heart at peace with it."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, ""Indeed, your heart has been sealed with faith, and indeed faith is given to the servant before the Quran."""
"157","A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am going to narrate to myself a hadith, and if I reach the heavens, I will be more eager to do so than if I were to speak with it."""
"158","And from him, on another occasion, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We find in ourselves what pleases us, we talk about it, and we have something that the sun has risen over it."" He said: ""Have you found that?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""That is the freshness of faith."""
"159","And even more so, I heard from my father that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you will say to the grape, 'This is the vineyard,' for indeed the vineyard is the Muslim man."""
"160","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""They will say, 'The grape', and indeed the grape is the heart of the believer."""
"161","By the One Who is with me, the example of a believer is like a piece of gold that has been blown upon by its owner, so it does not change or decrease. By the One Who is with me, the example of a believer is like a gazelle that has eaten good and clean food, and has stored it, and has given birth, so it does not break or spoil."
"162","The example of a believer is like that of a sprout of grass, which comes out in the morning and dries up in the evening, and the example of a disbeliever is like that of a dry tree stump, which remains dry until it is cut down."
"163","The example of a believer is like that of a horse that is ridden, then it returns to its original state. And indeed, the believer is ridden, then he returns to his faith."
"164","The Islam is a means, it does not ride except on a means."
"165","I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Faith will become strange and will return as it began. Good luck on that day to the people of the evening when time is corrupted. And that which my father's portion is in his hand will surely be divided between these two mosques, just as the living creature is divided in its womb."""
